{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "forescout-eyeinspect",
  "description": "Three hosts with alerts, services and firmware software. Asserts the hosts request carries full=true, which is what makes the Full-only properties (software, patches, open_ports, cves, main_role, purdue_level, criticality, main_vendor_model, firmware_version) present at all.\n\nsort_field must be ABSENT: `id` is not one of the accepted sort_field values in the API Guide, and with the parameter omitted the guide specifies the result is sorted by ID only, ascending -- exactly the order the walk needs.\n\nAlerts are fetched for every host, including host 9002. alert_count is not a Host record field (it appears only in the sort_field enum), so it is never present on real data and no short-circuit keyed on it can fire; 9002's alerts call is asserted present rather than absent, which is what a real Command Center does.\n\nThe hosts here deliberately carry OFF-CONTRACT value shapes -- purdue_level '1', criticality 'high', security_risk 'high' -- to prove a Command Center or a hand-edited record outside the documented domain still imports: the raw value survives as a custom attribute and simply produces no tag. vendor-schema.json covers the documented shapes.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "username": "fixture-operator",
    "password": "fixture-password",
    "last_seen_days": "0",
    "include_alerts": "true",
    "include_cve_details": "false"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "name": "hosts",
      "match": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/hosts"
      },
      "responses": [
